               DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION DELIVERS
            OpenVMS AFFINITY WAVE ONE FOR THE ENTERPRISE


  64-Bit OpenVMS Version 7.0, New Transaction Processing Software,
      Client/Server Tools & System Integration Services Provide
   Wave One Seamless Integration of OpenVMS & Windows NT Operating
             Systems for Enterprise Computing Solutions


SAN FRANCISCO, Calif., December 4, 1995 --  Digital Equipment 
Corporation and its partners today announce the first wave of 
products and services that facilitate the integration of OpenVMS and 
Windows NT.  These capabilities make it increasingly easy to 
develop, deploy, integrate and manage applications across both 
platforms in a three-tier client/server environment.

Being announced today at the Digital Equipment Computer User Society 
(DECUS) in San Francisco on December 4-6, 1995 are the following:

     o	OpenVMS Version 7.0 -- mission-critical 64-bit operating 
        system enhancements for the unlimited high-end

     o	Very Large Memory (VLM) capabilities with support from 
        Oracle Rdb7 and planned future support from Oracle7

     o	Three-tier client/server Fault Tolerant Transaction 
        Processing for Windows NT and for combined Windows NT & 
        OpenVMS environments

     o	Affinity development tools and complete development 
        environments from both Digital and partners

     o	Implementation Services to assist customers in deploying the 
        Affinity environment

     With the delivery of Affinity Wave One, current OpenVMS 
customers can easily add Windows NT servers -- along with Windows 
NT's huge application library -- to their computing environment.  
Windows NT users can easily add OpenVMS back-end servers to create 
Windows-based solutions with true 24X365 availability, disaster-
tolerance and scalability to the world's largest clusters.

     "What we've done here is mesh OpenVMS and Windows NT together 
so that customers can enjoy the scalability, reliability and 
cost-effectiveness they need while making a software investment in 
the operating environment of the future," said Wes Melling, vice 
president of Digital's OpenVMS Systems Business Group.  "In 
addition, they can enjoy this superior combination on the high-
performance, low-cost hardware platform of Alpha," said Melling. 

Delivering the Unlimited High-End: 64-Bit OpenVMS Version 7.0 

     OpenVMS provides extended capabilities for Windows NT users and 
applications in a client/server environment.  The latest release of 
OpenVMS delivers 64-bit data addressing on Alpha -- the leading 
64-bit hardware platform.  With this combination, customers are able 
to reap the full benefits of bullet-proof computing for data-
intensive applications such as micromarketing, data warehousing and 
on-line transaction processing. 

     Another significant addition in Version 7.0 of OpenVMS is Very 
Large Memory, or VLM.  VLM capabilities enable databases to run up 
to 200 times as fast as conventional 32-bit databases.  Digital, a 
leader in the emerging VLM/VLDB market, offers 64-bit support now on 
both OpenVMS and Digital UNIX computing environments. 

     In addition, Oracle Corporation is demonstrating support of 
OpenVMS Version 7.0 with the introduction here at DECUS of Oracle 
Rdb7 -- a 64-bit VLM implementation that brings OpenVMS users 
order-of-magnitude performance increases already demonstrated on 
Digital UNIX with Oracle7.  Oracle is also announcing today a 
commitment to deliver Oracle7 on OpenVMS V7.0 in the near future.

Delivering New High-Speed Data Back-Up Capability: Spiralog 
Version 1.0

     OpenVMS Version 7.0 offers fast, on-line back-up with Spiralog 
Version 1.0 -- a new 64-bit log-structured file system with a 
10-Terabyte design center.  The new file system is up to two times 
faster then the previous Files-11 file systems, and existing 
applications can run completely unchanged.  Spiralog is designed
for high-availability and is a fully clustered file system with 
transparent server fail-over, load balancing, compatibility with 
shadowing, striping and RAID 5.
Delivering New Windows NT Transaction Processing & Client/Server 
Tools for Affinity

     As key components of the Affinity program, Digital is 
delivering the first mission-critical transaction processing 
capabilities for Windows NT.  Included are the following new 
products:

ACMSxp V1.0 for Windows NT and ACMSxp V2.0 for OpenVMS

     ACMSxp is used by customers to develop, deploy and manage 
distributed client/server transaction processing applications.  
ACMSxp is available across OpenVMS, Windows NT or Digital UNIX-based 
systems and uses industry standard DCE.  ACMSxp V1.0 is the first 
industry tested, mission-critical TP software for Windows NT, and it 
is easily integrated with the OpenVMS environment.

Reliable Transaction Router V3.1 for Windows NT

     Digital's Reliable Transaction Router (RTR) is wide-area 
fault-tolerant middleware with transaction integrity.  RTR is for 
business applications that require the ability to execute 
transactions reliably, in real time, without any interrupt of 
service, across widely distributed systems.  RTR is deployed in
several of the world's stock exchanges, transportation systems, 
ticketing agencies and other environments that cannot afford to have 
a single moment of downtime. The delivery of RTR for Windows NT will 
allow customers to build fault-tolerant networks of Windows NT-based 
systems that are easily integrated with RTR on OpenVMS.

     Both ACMSxp and RTR use the three-tier client/server model for 
application architectures.  Digital customers in over 15,000 sites 
already have three-tier client/server systems in operation, making 
Digital the unquestioned leader in this emerging technology.

DECADMIRE V3.0, the ACMS Family Development Tool

     DECADMIRE, an application development tool from Digital, 
provides a vehicle for developers to quickly and easily design, 
develop, prototype, and test applications for the Microsoft Windows 
and  the Digital ACMS family of products. DECADMIRE generates ODBC, 
ACMS and ACMSxp (including STDL and DCE) applications in addition to 
Microsoft Visual Basic, DEC C, COBOL, FORTRAN, or Pascal source 
code.

     With DECADMIRE designers and developers can work individually 
or in teams to deliver three-tier client/server applications.  
DECADMIRE also extends the Microsoft Visual Basic environment to 
support mission critical applications and will be available in March 
of 1996.

Delivering New Development Tools for Affinity Application Providers

     Digital, Microsoft and their partners are collaborating to 
support multiple styles for creating applications on Windows NT and 
for deployment on both Windows NT and OpenVMS.  A number of 
Digital's premier software partners are introducing application 
development tools, databases, software tools, financial, health care
and other applications for the Affinity environment.  A number of 
these applications will ship shortly, and will support the 
integrated environment of Windows NT and OpenVMS.

     For Affinity Wave One, Digital has focused on partnering with 
software developers that deliver tools and applications for large 
Windows-based environments that require the strengths of OpenVMS.
Delivering New Services for Affinity

     Digital is announcing the availability of 31 System Integration 
Services designed to support the Affinity environment, which 
include:

     o	Services to align business and IT strategies
     o	Services to build an Affinity client/server infrastructure
     o	Services to integrate and migrate to the new environment
     o	Services for Affinity management and operations consulting

     Digital is also announcing the availability of new services 
from leading service providers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
