              DIGITAL OPENS DATABASE TECHNOLOGY CENTER
                  SUPPORTING TRANSITION TO 64-BIT,
                 VERY LARGE MEMORY (VLM64) COMPUTING


    ..Offers customers database optimization and VLM64 expertise;
 supports software partners with cooperative engineering programs...


MAYNARD, Mass., December 12, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today opened the doors to its new Database Technology Center (DBTC), 
located in Palo Alto, Calif., strengthening the company's position 
as the leading provider of 64-bit Very Large Memory (VLM64) 
solutions for commercial computing. The DBTC offers world-class 
database technology expertise designed to help customers capitalize 
on the performance and productivity advantages afforded by Digital's 
VLM64 technology and that of its database software partners.

     Informix, Oracle, and Sybase are combining the power of their 
VLM64 database solutions with the power of Digital's 64-bit 
AlphaServer systems to offer their customers record-setting database 
performance and memory capabilities. Through the DBTC, Digital and 
its partners are working cooperatively to help customers maximize 
the strategic use of the latest database designs and to solve 
problems associated with higher application loads.

     "Digital is at the forefront in delivering high-performance 
enterprise computing solutions," said James O'Gara, Digital vice 
president of the Database Market Development Group. "Our 64-bit 
AlphaServer systems and 64-bit Digital UNIX and OpenVMS operating 
systems, coupled with the VLM64 database technologies offered by 
our partners, provide business with the power and performance required 
for data-intensive applications such as data warehousing and on-line 
transaction processing. The Database Technology Center will assist our 
partners in addressing real-world challenges and developing solutions 
that will ensure them a long-term competitive edge."

     According to O'Gara, "The opening of the DBTC is a tremendous 
boost to our strategy to remain the leader in VLM64 technology. This 
facility is a rich resource for optimizing database performance and 
provides our sales organization a powerful resource for delivering 
enterprise-wide business solutions to our customers."

Competitive VLM64-based Information Solutions 

     Digital's Database Technology Center offers customers and 
software partners a resource for developing, optimizing and 
benchmarking VLM64-based information solutions. The facility is 
equipped with Digital's scalable family of 64-bit AlphaServer 
systems for enterprise, departmental and workgroup computing 
applications. It also provides database engineering expertise for 
analyzing and optimizing database performance, evaluating 
applications that run on a database, and advising customers on 
new developments in high-performance database designs.

     Digital's VLM64 technology dramatically improves database and 
application performance by raising the amount of information that 
can be stored in memory.  All 32-bit systems are effectively limited 
to 2 Gbytes of memory.  AlphaServer 8400 systems store up to 14 
Gbytes of data in memory today, with greater memory capacity planned 
for the future.

     Customers across a broad range of industries, such as health 
care, retailing, telecommunications and banking, view their adoption 
of Digital's VLM64 solutions as a key competitive advantage.

     Baxter Healthcare, for example, replaced its IBM mainframes 
with AlphaServer 8400 enterprise systems running SAP R/3 and the 
Oracle7 VLM64 database.

     The American Society of Civil Engineers replaced its Unisys 
mainframe with an AlphaServer 8000 system, Digital UNIX 64-bit 
operating system and the Oracle7 VLM64 database.

     Interested customers should contact Digital's Palo Alto 
Database Technology Center by calling Jim Young, Digital manager of 
the DBTC, at 415-617-3673.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
