                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
     DECLARES REGULAR CASH DIVIDEND ON SERIES A PREFERRED STOCK


MAYNARD, Mass., December 19, 1995  -- The Board of Directors of 
Digital Equipment Corporation (NYSE::DEC) has declared a regular 
cash dividend on its Series A 8 7/8% Cumulative Preferred Stock for 
the period from October 16, 1995 through January 15, 1996.  The 
dividend is equivalent to $0.5546875 per depositary share.  Each 
depositary share represents ownership of one-fourth of a share of 
Series A 8 7/8% Cumulative Preferred Stock, par value $1.00 per 
share, issued March 21, 1994.

     Dividends will be paid on January 16, 1996 to stockholders of 
record at the close of business on January 1, 1996.  The dividend 
payment for the period totals $8,875,000 for four million shares of 
Preferred Stock outstanding.

