              DIGITAL DELIVERS HIGH PERFORMING STORAGE
                      MANAGEMENT SOFTWARE TOOLS


 Yields Unprecedented Investment Protection and Reduced Storage Costs


MAYNARD, Mass., December 20, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today unveiled two OpenVMS software products that underscore the 
company's continuing commitment to provide customers with storage 
management software tools that support true heterogeneous 
environments.

     Both the new POLYCENTER Archive/Backup (PAB) for OpenVMS 
Version 1.1 and the POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem (SMF) 
for OpenVMS Version 1.2 combine robust features with measurable 
performance improvements, resulting in software tools that help 
users simplify the administration of network computing, protect 
their mission-critical data and manage the data consistently. Now, 
customers operating in Alpha and mixed Alpha and VAX environments, 
as well as VAX environments alone, can take advantage of these
improvements.

     "Companies today are faced with a rapid increase of information 
to be managed within both file systems and databases, as well as 
with increased pressure to control or decrease storage management 
costs," stated Tom Shea, senior product manager with Digital's 
Storage Management Software Group.  "Our software tools for a 
growing number of platforms help solve this dilemma.  
Digital offers the industry's most complete suite of storage 
management software products for OpenVMS users.  Plus, we help 
reduce the overall cost of storage ownership and further maximize 
users' OpenVMS storage hardware investments."

POLYCENTER Archive/Backup for OpenVMS Version 1.1

     PAB Version 1.1, the first POLYCENTER Archive/Backup tool to 
provide Alpha support, offers a full range of features that make 
storage management more efficient -- now, backups can be conducted 
up to five times faster than previous versions allowed.  These 
features include:

     o 	remote and unattended backup,

     o 	automatic, flexible scheduling of backup and archive 
        operations,

     o 	user-level restore through on-line catalogs of backed-up and 
        archived files,

     o 	sophisticated media life-cycle management,

     o 	and automatic failure recovery in VMS cluster environments.

     PAB Version 1.1 is a major component in VAX and Alpha data 
center environments operating 24 hours a day, seven days a week.  
For increased ease of use, PAB also features a more intuitive 
graphical user interface and an out-of-the-box configuration.

     Following on its long tradition of ensuring investment 
protection, Digital designed PAB as a follow-on product to its SLS 
for OpenVMS tool and has included PAB Version 1.1 in the same kit as 
SLS Version 2.6.  For added investment protection, PAB features 
superior SLS-to-PAB migration tools, operates with SLS licenses and 
allows users to restore SLS-created savesets. PAB also shares media 
management capabilities with Digital's other storage management 
software products, allowing for integration into the same environment.

POLYCENTER Sequential Media Filesystem for OpenVMS Version 1.2

     Also introduced today, SMF for OpenVMS Version 1.2 provides an 
advanced tape file system that is unique in the OpenVMS market -- 
alternative methods cannot match its high functionality and ease of 
use.  The software allows users with mixed Alpha and VAX 
environments to access and manipulate files stored on magnetic tape 
using the same interface currently used to manipulate files on 
magnetic disk.  This makes the function as easy and convenient as 
using disk media.  SMF Version 1.2 for OpenVMS also eliminates the 
commercial database prerequisite, lowering the cost of using the 
product and making it fully-functional out-of-the-box for easy 
installation.

Availability and Ordering

     POLYCENTER Archive/Backup Versions 1.1 for VAX and Alpha are 
included in the Storage Library System V2.6 for VAX and Alpha kits, 
available through Digital's sales offices and business partners.  
Server licenses for PAB Version 1.1 range from $2,495 to $9,800 and 
Remote licenses run from $495 to $1,980.  The POLYCENTER Sequential 
Media Filesystem Version 1.2 is available on the November/December 
1995 OpenVMS Layered Product CD-ROM, and is also available on 
traditional TK50 and 9TK tapes.  Workgroup licenses for SMF Version 
1.2 are $995, and Enterprise Licenses are $3995.

